1
00:00:00,448 --> 00:00:03,880
So how can we now get HTMX to automatically

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:06,654
send that GET request every 5 seconds?

3
00:00:07,872 --> 00:00:10,085
Well, for that, we need to adjust the

4
00:00:10,438 --> 00:00:10,983
trigger

5
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:13,404
of this GET request.

6
00:00:14,463 --> 00:00:17,509
Remember that the default trigger is the

7
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:21,774
most obvious event for the element on which

8
00:00:21,999 --> 00:00:24,051
this attribute is added. And for an

9
00:00:24,147 --> 00:00:26,168
unordered list, like for most elements,

10
00:00:26,488 --> 00:00:27,611
that's a click event.

11
00:00:28,316 --> 00:00:30,415
That's why at the moment we send this

12
00:00:30,415 --> 00:00:32,338
request when we click on this element.

13
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:35,608
But now I actually wanna change that trigger

14
00:00:35,624 --> 00:00:39,341
and we can do that by using hx-trigger.

15
00:00:40,752 --> 00:00:42,707
But I don't wanna change it to some other

16
00:00:42,819 --> 00:00:44,453
user event. Instead,

17
00:00:44,998 --> 00:00:46,248
I wanna change it to some

18
00:00:46,905 --> 00:00:49,325
automated polling mechanism.

19
00:00:50,287 --> 00:00:52,947
And turns out that HTMX got support for

20
00:00:52,947 --> 00:00:55,719
that. Instead of specifying an event like

21
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:58,091
mouseenter or click here,

22
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:00,834
you can also specify specify every

23
00:01:01,735 --> 00:01:04,001
and then some time period like 2s

24
00:01:04,645 --> 00:01:07,892
for 2 seconds or 5 seconds, which is what I

25
00:01:08,021 --> 00:01:08,375
want here.

26
00:01:09,939 --> 00:01:12,438
And you can learn about all the possible

27
00:01:12,922 --> 00:01:15,970
triggers and trigger modifiers here in the

28
00:01:15,970 --> 00:01:16,933
official documentation.

29
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:19,729
There you learn about this polling

30
00:01:20,018 --> 00:01:20,661
mechanism,

31
00:01:21,866 --> 00:01:23,842
but you will also learn that you could, for

32
00:01:23,874 --> 00:01:26,503
example, add the once modifier to only

33
00:01:26,535 --> 00:01:29,294
listen to the first event of a certain type

34
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:33,118
that occurs, that you could add delays and

35
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:33,344
more,

36
00:01:33,876 --> 00:01:35,845
whatever you need for the application you

37
00:01:35,894 --> 00:01:36,427
are building.

38
00:01:37,576 --> 00:01:40,100
Now, in my case here, I'm interested in that

39
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,591
polling mechanism and that works with help

40
00:01:42,591 --> 00:01:44,990
of that every keyword, which you add here

41
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:47,201
followed by the timeframe.

42
00:01:48,633 --> 00:01:50,880
Now, you can also write more advanced code

43
00:01:50,913 --> 00:01:53,990
here and for example, also combine multiple

44
00:01:54,006 --> 00:01:54,299
triggers

45
00:01:54,848 --> 00:01:57,384
But for our example here, this is all we

46
00:01:57,384 --> 00:01:57,597
need.

47
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:02,755
Well, and with that code added, if you now

48
00:02:02,965 --> 00:02:05,676
reload, you will see that after 5 seconds,

49
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:09,297
those suggested places will be swapped out

50
00:02:09,426 --> 00:02:10,941
for 2 different places.

51
00:02:11,682 --> 00:02:14,324
And then after 5 seconds, we again have them

52
00:02:14,437 --> 00:02:17,801
being replaced and so on. So now HTMX is

53
00:02:17,979 --> 00:02:20,490
polling for new places every 5 seconds. 5

54
00:02:20,779 --> 00:02:21,293
seconds.

55
00:02:22,352 --> 00:02:24,245
And of course, we can still add places from

56
00:02:24,277 --> 00:02:26,508
up there. Then we'll automatically refetch

57
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:29,059
these places, but the polling mechanism will

58
00:02:29,123 --> 00:02:32,349
stay active because we specified it here on

59
00:02:32,397 --> 00:02:34,338
the unordered list. And we're never

60
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:36,585
replacing this unordered list item here

61
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:40,211
because when we do return it, like here when

62
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:40,436
we

63
00:02:41,206 --> 00:02:44,191
added a new place to the dream places, we

64
00:02:44,191 --> 00:02:46,758
perform that out-of-band swap such that we

65
00:02:46,983 --> 00:02:49,703
only replace the content, the children of

66
00:02:49,719 --> 00:02:52,234
this unordered list with the content defined

67
00:02:52,234 --> 00:02:54,378
here and not the list as a whole.

68
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,569
And that's therefore how you can set up

69
00:02:57,634 --> 00:02:59,407
polling with HTMX.
